sentences.t:
Fasta terçer día nol pueden acordar;
ellos partiendo estas ganançias grandes,
nol pueden fazer comer un muesso de pan.

sentences.l:
Until third day not-him they-can bring-round;
they dividing these gains great,
not-him they-can make eat a morsel of bread.

sentences.t:
Mas quanto avedes perdido e yo gané en canpo,
sabet, non daré a vos [de ello] un dinero malo;
ca huebos me lo he pora estos que comigo andan lazrados.

sentences.l:
But as-much you-have lost and I won in field,
know-ye, not I-will-give to you of it a penny bad;
for need to-me it I-have for these who with-me go toiling.

sentences.t:
Prendiendo de vos e de otros ir nos hemos pagando;
abremos esta vida mientra ploguiere al Padre santo,
commo que ira a de rey e de tierra es echado.”

sentences.l:
Taking from you and from others go ourselves we-will paying;
we-will-have this life while it-may-please to-the Father holy,
as one-who anger has of king and from land is cast-out.”

“If you it-may-please, my Çid, of going we-are ready;
order-us to-give the beasts and we-will-ride quickly:
from-the day that I-was count not I-dined so of good will,
the relish that thereof I-have not will-be forgotten.”

sentences.t:
Si vos viniere emiente que quisiéredes vengallo,
si me viniéredes buscar, fa[zedme antes] mand[ado];
o me dexaredes de lo vuestro, o de lo mio levaredes algo.”

sentences.l:
If to-you may-come to-mind that you-might-want to-avenge-it,
if me you-come to-seek, make-me before message;
either me you-will-leave of the yours, or of the mine you-will-carry something.”

sentences.t:
—“Folguedes, ya mio Çid, sodes en vuestro salvo.
Pagado vos he por todo aqueste año;
de venirvos buscar sol non será penssado.”

sentences.l:
—“Rest-you, O my Çid, you-are in your safety.
Paid you I-have for all this year;
of coming-you to-seek not-even not will-be thought.”
